//RS /// #2252: a generated codec is a top-level item of the module that DECLARES
//RS /// the type, so it lowers under that module's canonical owner while every
//RS /// expression inside that module still names the type by its local leaf. The
//RS /// default `jet run` lens must resolve both spellings instead of deopting with
//RS /// an unsupported `Encode`/`Decode` body.
//RS ///
//RS /// The consumer side of the same seam: a cross-module call answers with the
//RS /// success view its own return lowering added, so every payload consumer --
//RS /// a field read, a codec's text argument, a builtin or user method receiver --
//RS /// must read through that view instead of refusing the value.
//RS #[test]
