//RS /// c109 (boxed recursive field read): reading a self-referential struct field
//RS /// (`t.child`, Rust type `Box<…>` via `cx.boxed_edges`) miscompiled — the read
//RS /// yielded a `Box<…>` where the unboxed type was wanted (rustc E0308). The fix
//RS /// derefs the `Box` (`(*(…))`) on a boxed-field read. With the read fixed, a
//RS /// recursive struct is now a covered VALUE type, so a fn that builds AND traverses
//RS /// a `Tree` (binds a boxed child, matches, recurses) routes through the TIR.
