//RS /// c109 Phase 6b: a `Shared<T>` value passed to a FREE (non-method) call inside a loop
//RS /// auto-clones the handle — `emit_call_args` emits `(…).clone()` (D-MEM1 S6: `Shared<T>`
//RS /// lowers to `jet_std::JetShared<T>`, a newtype with its own cheap-handle `Clone` impl,
//RS /// not a bare `Arc<T>` — was `Arc::clone(&…)` before this stage) and the receiving
//RS /// `Shared<T>` `Read` param borrows it (`&(…)`). The gate previously excluded
//RS /// `shared_auto_clone` on plain `Call` args, routing `loop_user`/`noop` through the AST
//RS /// path; both now route through the TIR with a byte-identical emit. A `Shared<T>` value
//RS /// has no surface constructor (it only ever arrives as a param), so this is a compile +
//RS /// byte-exact-Rust assertion (the same surface `tests/ownership.rs` and `tests/ui_lint`
//RS /// exercise) rather than a build+run. rustc accepting the output proves I2.
